vms-f97 (2/2): alpha-dec-vms — VMS DST routine-begin entry address uses the
resolved (transparent-alias-decorated) name, matching the emitted ..en label.

Second site of the same codegen-consistency defect fixed by
0001-vms-f97-alpha-en-label-decorated-name.patch. write_rtnbeg() in the VMS
debug/traceback writer builds the routine-begin ENTRY ADDRESS by concatenating
"..en" to the RAW routine name (rtnname), then emits it via write_debug_addr()
(-> assemble_name()). For a recognized OpenVMS C-RTL *definition* the code entry
label is decc$<name>..en (config/alpha/alpha.cc after patch 0001), but this
record referenced <name>..en — a label that does not exist — so GAS rejected the
object even after the .pdesc was fixed (e.g. `strlen..en` vs `decc$strlen..en`;
"redefined symbol cannot be used on reloc"). This DST record is emitted for
every VMS function, so it blocks the C-RTL definitions regardless of -g.

Fix: resolve rtnname via assemble_name_resolve() (the routine assemble_name uses)
BEFORE appending "..en", so the entry address matches the real label. The
procedure-descriptor address just below already resolves correctly (it passes
rtnname straight to assemble_name), and the human-readable routine NAME field
correctly stays the source name. Consistency-only; the decoration behavior itself
is unchanged.

Clean-room (Rule 8): derived from public GCC source + observed cc1/GAS output.

--- a/gcc/vmsdbgout.cc
+++ b/gcc/vmsdbgout.cc
@@ -654,7 +654,16 @@
 
   rtnname = funcnam_table[rtnnum];
   rtnnamelen = strlen (rtnname);
-  rtnentryname = concat (rtnname, "..en", NULL);
+  /* vms-f97 (OVMX): the routine-begin ENTRY ADDRESS must reference the same
+     resolved (transparent-alias-decorated) entry label the code emits in
+     alpha_start_function (config/alpha/alpha.cc) -- decc$<name>..en for a
+     recognized OpenVMS C-RTL name (config/vms/vms.cc).  Building it from the
+     raw name produced `strlen..en`, a label that does not exist, so GAS
+     rejected the object.  assemble_name_resolve () applies the alias exactly
+     as assemble_name () does for the procedure-descriptor address emitted
+     just below (which stays rtnname); the human-readable routine NAME field
+     further down also, correctly, stays the source name.  */
+  rtnentryname = concat (assemble_name_resolve (rtnname), "..en", NULL);
 
   if (!strcmp (rtnname, "main"))
     {
